From b7204583524091735367cd98ee488fe543e10473 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anun333 <anun333@posteo.net>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:02:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] libclc: fix atanpi(-0.0) for doubles

atanpi_fp64 took the result's sign with

    return x == v ? z : -z;

where v is fabs(x). For x = -0.0 that test is true, because -0.0 == +0.0
in IEEE 754, so the positive branch was taken and atanpi(-0.0) returned
+0.0 instead of -0.0.

Take the sign bitwise instead, which is what atanpi_fp32.cl already does.
z is non-negative on every path that reaches the return except NaN, where
it is x and keeps its own sign under the OR.

Reported by math_edge_cases (OpenCL-CTS#2665); the float version already
passed. libclc/atan_fp64.cl carries the same line, but the host CPU
kernel library builds atan from sleef-pocl/atan.cl, so that copy is not
reachable there -- left alone rather than changed blind. Checked
atan/asin/asinpi/tan/sinh/atanh/erf at -0.0 on this device: all already
correct.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (Claude Code)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4801768548d08848413586d5b63ec1e52f38a0ae)
---
 lib/kernel/libclc/atanpi_fp64.cl | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/kernel/libclc/atanpi_fp64.cl b/lib/kernel/libclc/atanpi_fp64.cl
index a9435acbf..f21b0f04a 100644
--- a/lib/kernel/libclc/atanpi_fp64.cl
+++ b/lib/kernel/libclc/atanpi_fp64.cl
@@ -99,5 +99,10 @@ _CL_OVERLOADABLE vtype atanpi(vtype x) {
     vtype z = isnan(x) ? x : (vtype)0.5;
     z = (v <= (vtype)0x1.0p+56) ? r : z;
     z = (v < (vtype)0x1.0p-26) ? vp : z;
-    return x == v ? z : -z;
+    // atanpi is odd, so the sign comes from x -- but x == fabs(x) is
+    // true for -0.0, so that test returned +0.0 for atanpi(-0.0). Take
+    // the sign bitwise instead, as atanpi_fp32.cl already does. z is
+    // non-negative here except for NaN, where it is x and keeps its own
+    // sign under the OR.
+    return as_vtype((as_itype(x) & (itype)SIGNBIT_DP64) | as_itype(z));
 }
